annotations:
  artifacthub.io/changes: "- kind: security\n  description: Fixed PHP2Shell (CVE-2026-109618,
    CVE-2026-109619) — image now requires Sury php7.4 >= 1:7.4.33-31, which backports
    the fix from PHP 8.2.35. The package changelog is kept in the image as evidence.\n
    \ links:\n    - name: CVE-2026-109618\n      url: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-109618\n
    \   - name: CVE-2026-109619\n      url: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-109619\n-
    kind: security\n  description: Disabled PHP session upload progress and pinned
    it via php_admin_flag so .htaccess cannot re-enable it — defense in depth for
    CVE-2026-109619 and mitigation for the not yet patched CVE-2026-115560.\n  links:\n
    \   - name: CVE-2026-115560\n      url: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-115560\n-
    kind: security\n  description: Fixed blueimp-file-upload CVE-2018-9206 — the vulnerable
    server handler is not shipped (FileManager uses its own upload handling), client
    scripts updated to 9.22.1, HTTP access to the handler path denied as a safeguard.\n
    \ links:\n    - name: CVE-2018-9206\n      url: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2018-9206\n-
    kind: fixed\n  description: Redirects such as /admin → /admin/ now use the public
    URL from cmsms_settings.host instead of http://<host>:8080.\n- kind: fixed\n  description:
    cmsms_app.strategy.type Recreate no longer fails with \"rollingUpdate may not
    be specified\".\n- kind: fixed\n  description: Fallback to older database configuration
    when available.\n- kind: changed\n  description: Changed Image Source to Debian
    Trixie (13).\n  \n"
